---
import Section from './Section.astro';
---

<Section id="questions" number="07" label="Questions" title="Questions.">
  <div class="list">
    <details>
      <summary>Does it replace Linear?</summary>
      <p>It can. Or sync with it. Dispatch is where agents work; your tracker stays current either way.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What agents does it run?</summary>
      <p>Claude Code today. More harnesses are coming.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Where does my code go?</summary>
      <p>Nowhere. Local by default. Opt into team sharing when you want it.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
      <p>Free to run locally. Bring your own agent.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  .list {
    max-width: 40rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  }
  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  }
  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding: var(--space-4) 0;
    font-weight: 500;
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  /* A plus that turns into a minus when the answer is open: the one bit of motion on the
     page, and it answers a click. */
  summary::after {
    content: '+';
    flex: none;
    width: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-weight: 400;
    text-align: center;
    transition: transform 160ms var(--ease-out-expo);
  }
  details[open] summary::after {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }
  details p {
    max-width: var(--site-measure);
    padding: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
</style>
